{"type":"message","id":"a03e5568","parentId":"f58b4d4b","timestamp":"2026-06-03T15:05:40.806Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The GET is working but POST /send is failing with error 1101. Let me try different approaches for the POST - maybe there's a specific JSON structure needed, or maybe the API endpoint path is different. Let me check if there's a different endpoint format or if the API key header name is different.\n\nActually wait - error 1101 is a Cloudflare Workers error code that typically means \"Worker exceeded memory limit\" or \"Worker CPU time limit exceeded\". This suggests the worker itself is having issues, not that the API key or payload is wrong.\n\nLet me try one more time with a very simple payload.","thinkingSignature":"e3ebb0fec97d7f1e461c60b51f2ad986ee369e4614e2884829b8f29ce99eb1ff"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_162c7bf8936e4dd4814eb763","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  --max-time 30 \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 15:00 UTC\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":216,"output":227,"cacheRead":21760,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22203,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780499136905,"responseId":"066f75c17d0f20f77afc69d202485904"}}
